SUMMARY:Venus\, Mercury\, Jupiter or waxing Moon with / aspecting the Sun 
 (user note)
DESCRIPTION:Date/Time (NY): 2027-04-20 07:01 EDT -> 2027-04-20 18:27 EDT\n
 Planetary condition: At start: Sun 05.91 deg Aries (Ashwini pada 2\; D9 T
 aurus)\, 0.976 deg/day | At end: Sun 06.37 deg Aries (Ashwini pada 2\; D9
  Taurus)\, 0.976 deg/day | Computed: separation from Sun at start: Venus 
 29.8 deg\, Mercury 9.2 deg\, Jupiter 106.9 deg\, Moon 174.1 deg\; value: 
 waxing Moon aspects (7th)\nAstrological rule: Venus\, Mercury or Jupiter 
 in the Sun's sign or casting drishti on it\, or the Moon doing so during 
 Shukla paksha.\nSource interpretation: Venus\, Mercury\, Jupiter or waxin
 g Moon with / aspecting the Sun (user note): Can trigger gold price hike 
 (Bullish)\nFinancial market significance: Can trigger gold price hike (Bu
 llish) -> Gold (XAUUSD / COMEX GC) (as the source states it\; not a forec
 ast)\nConditions & qualifications: Aspect = whole-sign graha drishti (Jup
 iter 5/7/9\, Saturn 3/7/10\, Rahu 7 - project convention\; Rahu's 7th fal
 ls on Ketu's sign)\; conjunction = same sign. Venus and Mercury can only 
 conjoin the Sun (they never get far enough to aspect it). | Conflict: TA 
 p.154 S34 A3 and the 2026 document's gold-bullish #2 make the Sun in Libr
 a with/aspected by malefics (Saturn\, Mars\, Rahu) BULLISH for gold\, and
  TA S34 A10 says a malefic aspect makes the Sun's rally stars MORE bullis
 h\; TA S34 B1 makes a benefic with the Sun on Anuradha bearish. Both sour
 ces are shown. | Mercury is never more than ~28 deg from the Sun\, so it 
 shares the Sun's sign for long stretches of the year.\nSource reference: 
 User note (project chat\, 20 Nov 2026\; Reference_materials/user_notes_go
 ld.md)\nCalculation method: Sidereal (Lahiri) whole sign of the body\; wi
 ndow bounded by its ingresses. Waxing = Shukla paksha (elongation 0-180 d
 eg). Window changes whenever the set of contacts changes. || Swiss Epheme
 ris (pyswisseph\, sepl/semo 18 files)\, sidereal Lahiri ayanamsha\, mean 
 lunar node\, whole-sign relationships\; condition sampled hourly and ever
 y boundary bisected to 30 seconds\; times shown in New York local time (E
