 o)\, 0.989 deg/day | At end: Sun 27.73 deg Virgo (Chitra pada 2\; D9 Virg
 o)\, 0.991 deg/day | Computed: separation from Sun at start: Venus 16.7 d
 eg\, Mercury 13.0 deg\, Jupiter 33.0 deg\, Moon 154.4 deg\; value: waxing
  Moon aspects (7th)\nAstrological rule: Venus\, Mercury or Jupiter in the
  Sun's sign or casting drishti on it\, or the Moon doing so during Shukla
  paksha.\nSource interpretation: Venus\, Mercury\, Jupiter or waxing Moon
  with / aspecting the Sun (user note): Can trigger gold price hike (Bulli
 sh)\nFinancial market significance: Can trigger gold price hike (Bullish)
  -> Gold (XAUUSD / COMEX GC) (as the source states it\; not a forecast)\n
 Conditions & qualifications: Aspect = whole-sign graha drishti (Jupiter 5
 /7/9\, Saturn 3/7/10\, Rahu 7 - project convention\; Rahu's 7th falls on 
 Ketu's sign)\; conjunction = same sign. Venus and Mercury can only conjoi
 n the Sun (they never get far enough to aspect it). | Conflict: TA p.154 
 S34 A3 and the 2026 document's gold-bullish #2 make the Sun in Libra with
 /aspected by malefics (Saturn\, Mars\, Rahu) BULLISH for gold\, and TA S3
 4 A10 says a malefic aspect makes the Sun's rally stars MORE bullish\; TA
  S34 B1 makes a benefic with the Sun on Anuradha bearish. Both sources ar
 e shown. | Mercury is never more than ~28 deg from the Sun\, so it shares
  the Sun's sign for long stretches of the year.\nSource reference: User n
 ote (project chat\, 20 Nov 2026\; Reference_materials/user_notes_gold.md)
 \nCalculation method: Sidereal (Lahiri) whole sign of the body\; window b
 ounded by its ingresses. Waxing = Shukla paksha (elongation 0-180 deg). W
 indow changes whenever the set of contacts changes. || Swiss Ephemeris (p
 yswisseph\, sepl/semo 18 files)\, sidereal Lahiri ayanamsha\, mean lunar 
 node\, whole-sign relationships\; condition sampled hourly and every boun
 dary bisected to 30 seconds\; times shown in New York local time (EST/EDT
